{
  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-intelligence-and-security-studies-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Intel & Security Studies Full Time Permanent - Faculty Unclassified $70,000 Add to favorites View favorites The Position The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Irregular warfare places difficult questions of intelligence, influence, and legitimacy at the center of the study of conflict. It demands attention to how states and nonstate actors mobilize populations, exploit uncertainty, and pursue political objectives through indirect means. This appointment offers the opportunity to advance scholarship on those questions while helping future practitioners develop the judgment to confront them. The Department and The Citadel Our department connects the intellectual breadth of the humanities and social sciences with the practical demands of intelligence. Its undergraduate and graduate degrees are certified by the International Association for Intelligence Education. Faculty combine active scholarship with professional experience, and the annual Day of Intrigue exercise brings students and intelligence practitioners together to work through complex national security scenarios. A new $250,000 federal award is supporting the Intelligence Futures and Judgment Lab and a deeper integration of wargaming into the curriculum. Students must weigh incomplete evidence, respond to competing interests, and take responsibility for their decisions. The successful candidate will have an opportunity to help shape this work, connecting research on irregular warfare with the development of students’ analytical judgment. The Citadel gives this work a distinctive home. A public senior military college in Charleston, it has ranked first among Regional Universities in the South in U.S. News & World Report for three consecutive years. Faculty teach cadets preparing to commission as military officers, as well as students pursuing civilian careers in intelligence and national security. These students may soon be responsible for leading others and making consequential assessments. Teaching here offers the opportunity to develop the intellectual discipline and ethical judgment they will bring to those responsibilities. Research and Teaching We welcome specializations in insurgency and counterinsurgency, resistance and unconventional warfare, political warfare, proxy conflict, special operations, terrorism and counterterrorism, or information operations and influence. Regional and methodological approaches are open. Candidates should connect their expertise to broader questions in intelligence and security studies. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in irregular warfare and broader intelligence and security studies, in person and online as assigned. Sustain an active research agenda and produce peer-reviewed scholarship appropriate to the rank of Assistant Professor. Develop applied learning experiences that challenge students to test assumptions, assess evidence, and defend their judgments. Mentor students, supervise research and applied projects, and contribute to curriculum development and assessment. Participate in departmental and college service and build appropriate connections with scholarly and practitioner communities. Required Qualifications A Ph.D. in intelligence studies, security studies, political science, international relations, history, public policy, or a closely related field. ABD candidates will be considered if the degree is completed prior to the beginning of the fall 2027 semester. Demonstrated expertise in irregular warfare, evidenced through research, teaching, or relevant professional work, and a clear agenda for continued scholarship. Evidence of, or strong potential for, effective college teaching and the ability to contribute to both undergraduate and graduate education. A commitment to close student mentorship, rigorous inquiry, constructive academic collaboration, and The Citadel’s mission of developing principled leaders. Preferred Qualifications Candidates may demonstrate strength in one or more of the following areas: Experience designing or facilitating wargames, simulations, or other forms of experiential learning. Research or professional experience connecting irregular warfare with intelligence analysis, intelligence operations, or national security policy. Regional expertise, relevant language skills, fieldwork, or research on the role of emerging technologies in irregular conflict. Experience teaching online, mentoring student research, or developing collaborative projects with government, military, academic, or private-sector partners. Appointment and Compensation The standard teaching load is four courses per semester (4/4). The Citadel offers state employee benefits. Application Instructions In addition to your online application, please submit the following materials: A cover letter describing the candidate’s qualifications and intended contribution to the department. A curriculum vitae. A research statement describing current work and future plans, up to two pages. A teaching statement addressing relevant courses, student learning, and approaches to applied instruction, up to two pages. Evidence of teaching effectiveness may be included if available. One scholarly writing sample. Names and contact information for three references. Letters may be requested later in the search. Review of applications will begin December 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Applications received by that date will receive full consideration. Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Melissa Graves, Chair of the Department of Intelligence and Security Studies, at mgraves2@citadel.edu . Located on the Charleston peninsula along the Ashley River, The Citadel offers an academic community within a city known for its history and cultural life. Content missing Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Political Science in International Relations and Comparative Politics & Middle East Area Studies Charleston Political Science The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina, is currently seeking to fill a tenure-track appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor in International Relations and Comparative Politics in the Department of Political Science. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-political-science-in-international-relations-and-comparative-politics-middle-east-area-studies-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Political Science in International Relations and Comparative Politics & Middle East Area Studies",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Political Science in International Relations and Comparative Politics & Middle East Area Studies - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Assistant Professor of Political Science in International Relations and Comparative Politics & Middle East Area Studies - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Political Science in International Relations and Comparative Politics & Middle East Area Studies Political Science Full Time Permanent - Faculty Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites Job Responsibilities: The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina, is currently seeking to fill a tenure-track appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor in International Relations and Comparative Politics in the Department of Political Science. The Citadel is a state-supported coeducational military college in historic downtown Charleston, South Carolina. We are committed to excellence in teaching with the expectation that faculty engage in consistent research and publication. The department offers a B.A. in Political Science with three subfields: American Government, International Politics and Military Affairs, and pre-Law and Legal Studies. The Department is home to approximately 140 undergraduate majors. In addition, the Department of Political Science offers a Master of Arts program in International Politics & Military Affairs (IPMA) and graduate courses related to a Master of Arts program in Social Science (MASS). A Ph.D. is preferred, but ABD eligible candidates who will finish their dissertation by August 2027 will be considered. Expertise in Middle Eastern area studies and International Political Economy is required with a preference for those with professional experience in a US government agency or equivalent international organization. Undergraduate teaching responsibilities include: Introduction to International Politics, Comparative Politics, American Foreign Policy, International Political Economy, and Middle Eastern Politics (regionally and country-specific). The ability to teach Comparative Foreign Policy would also be an asset. Successful candidates will also be expected to teach online courses related to the two Master of Arts Programs. Teaching expectations are a four-four load. Service responsibilities for this position include helping direct our Masters in International & Military Affairs (IPMA) degree. Please include a CV, cover letter, three letters of recommendation, and writing sample in your online application. The Political Science department will begin considering applications on January 15, 2027. To learn more about The Citadel and its programs please visit our website at www.citadel.edu . To find more information on the Department of Political Science, you can visit us at http://www.citadel.edu/root/politicalscience . Start Your Application First Name (required) a00ac480 Last Name (required) 5f34f907 Email (required) 29065e75 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/tenure-track-assistant-or-associate-professor-in-sports-management-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor in Sports Management",
      "description": "Tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor in Sports Management - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor in Sports Management - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor in Sports Management School Science and Mathematics Full Time Permanent - Faculty Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites Tenure Track Assistant or Associate Professor in Sport Management The Citadel, the Military College of South Carolina, invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-track position in Sport Management at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor in the Department of Health and Human Performance. The anticipated start date is Fall 2027, with the possibility of an earlier start in January 2027, depending on candidate availability and departmental needs. Founded in 1842 and located in historic Charleston, South Carolina, The Citadel is a coeducational, state-assisted college dedicated to excellence in educating principled leaders. Total enrollment is approximately 3,900 students, including approximately 2,400 members of the South Carolina Corps of Cadets and students enrolled in graduate, evening undergraduate, College Transfer Program, and online offerings. In the U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings, The Citadel is ranked No. 1 among Regional Universities in the South for the second consecutive year, No. 1 among Public Regional Universities in the South for the 15th consecutive year, and No. 1 among Best Colleges for Veterans in the South for the eighth consecutive year. One of seven departments in the Swain Family School of Science and Mathematics, Health and Human Performance offers a B.S. in Sport Management for the South Carolina Corps of Cadets and an online M.A. in Sport Management. The department also offers B.S. degrees in Exercise Science and Strength and Conditioning and an M.S. in Health and Human Performance. The department emphasizes excellent teaching, student mentorship, and applied learning, while supporting faculty scholarship and professional development. The Citadel provides internal funding for faculty research, professional development, and travel, and offers competitive benefits. Compensation is competitive and commensurate with credentials and experience. A 12:1 student-to-faculty ratio and an average undergraduate class size of approximately 20 support close engagement with students. Position Responsibilities Teaching • Teach undergraduate and online graduate courses across the Sport Management curriculum, with assignments based on program needs and the candidate’s expertise. • Potential teaching areas include Introduction to Sport Management, Sociocultural Aspects of Sport, Sport Law, Leadership in Sport Organizations, International Sport Management, Sport Governance, Sport Communications, internships, and esports. • Develop new courses and contribute to curriculum review and improvement. Research and Scholarship • Maintain scholarly productivity consistent with departmental and college expectations for tenure and promotion. • Mentor undergraduate and graduate students in research and scholarly activities. Advising Service and Professional Engagement • Advise and mentor undergraduate and graduate students in their academic and professional development. • Participate in faculty governance and serve on departmental, school, and college committees. • Develop and maintain industry partnerships, internship sites, and other experiential learning opportunities for students. Minimum Qualifications An earned doctorate in Sport Management or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Preferred Qualifications • Demonstrated teaching experience and effectiveness appropriate to the rank sought, with the ability to teach across multiple areas of Sport Management. • Experience mentoring undergraduate and graduate students and engaging them in research. • A record of scholarly publications appropriate to the rank sought. • Experience developing courses and curricula. • Experience developing or maintaining industry partnerships and internship sites. In addition to the online application, applicants should submit the following materials: • A cover letter addressing the minimum qualifications and applicable preferred qualifications. • An updated curriculum vitae. • A narrative describing the candidate’s teaching philosophy and plans for scholarly activity. • A list of at least three professional references, including two who can speak to the candidate’s teaching ability and experience. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questions about the position may be directed to Dr. Myungwoo Lee, Search Committee Chair, at mlee12@citadel.edu or (843) 953-4852. Mailing address: The Citadel, 171 Moultrie Street, Charleston, SC 29409. Start Your Application First Name (required) 45d3ad12 Last Name (required) 64b69a7a Email (required) d64f559d Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/nursing-instructor-pediatrics-and-medical-surgical-nursing-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Nursing Instructor - Pediatrics and Medical Surgical Nursing",
      "description": "Nursing Instructor - Pediatrics and Medical Surgical Nursing - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Nursing Instructor - Pediatrics and Medical Surgical Nursing - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Nursing Instructor - Pediatrics and Medical Surgical Nursing Nursing Full Time Permanent - Faculty Unclassified 80,000 Add to favorites View favorites The Citadel, the Military College of South Carolina, invites applications for two full-time, nine-month Instructor positions in the Swain Department of Nursing beginning Fall 2027. One position will focus on pediatric nursing and the other on medical-surgical nursing. An earlier start in January 2027 is possible for the pediatrics position, depending on candidate availability and departmental needs. We seek faculty committed to excellent teaching, close student mentorship, and preparing nurses to lead and serve in professional practice. Salary and benefits are competitive. Founded in 1842 and located in historic Charleston, South Carolina, The Citadel is a public, coeducational senior military college dedicated to educating and developing principled leaders. Total enrollment is approximately 3,900 students, including approximately 2,400 members of the South Carolina Corps of Cadets, with additional students enrolled in graduate, evening undergraduate, College Transfer Program, and online offerings. In the 2027 U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings, The Citadel is ranked No. 1 among Regional Universities in the South for the third consecutive year, No. 1 among Public Regional Universities in the South for the 16th consecutive year, and No. 1 among Best Colleges for Veterans in the South for the ninth consecutive year. One of seven departments in the Swain Family School of Science and Mathematics, the Swain Department of Nursing offers a Bachelor of Science in Nursing (BSN) accredited by the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education (CCNE). Established in 2017, the program offers face-to-face instruction through both a day program for the South Carolina Corps of Cadets and an evening degree-completion program. Small classes support personalized learning and direct faculty engagement with students. The Citadel’s 12:1 student-to-faculty ratio and average undergraduate class size of approximately 20 support close engagement with students. The Citadel provides internal funding for faculty professional development and travel. Position Responsibilities Teach in the classroom and clinical setting, with pediatric nursing as the primary responsibility for one position and medical-surgical nursing as the primary responsibility for the other. Teach additional courses according to departmental needs and faculty expertise. Assignments may include fundamentals of nursing, health assessment, community health, nursing leadership, or other nursing courses. Mentor students and support their development of clinical judgment, professional skills, and readiness for nursing practice. Participate in departmental and college service. Required Qualifications An earned master’s degree in nursing. An active, unencumbered license to practice as a registered nurse in South Carolina or eligibility to obtain South Carolina RN licensure. Nursing practice experience in the relevant specialty, including at least two years of experience in pediatric nursing for the pediatrics position or medical-surgical nursing for the medical-surgical position. Preferred Qualifications Current clinical practice in the specialty relevant to the position. Certification in nursing practice or as a nurse educator. At least two years of teaching experience in an academic environment. At least five years of clinical practice experience as a registered nurse. Experience with nursing simulation and CCNE accreditation. Experience as a military nurse. Experience or interest in delivering online curricula. Application Instructions Applicants should submit the following materials: A cover letter identifying the position sought and addressing the required and applicable preferred qualifications. An updated curriculum vitae. A narrative describing the candidate’s teaching philosophy and approach to classroom and clinical instruction. Contact information for at least three professional references, including two who can speak to the candidate’s teaching ability and experience. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until both positions are filled. Start Your Application First Name (required) 5cdab49c Last Name (required) 33fd6bbc Email (required) f8a3061b Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/tenure-track-assistant-or-associate-professor-of-physics-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Assistant or Associate Professor of Physics",
      "description": "Tenure-Track Assistant or Associate Professor of Physics - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Tenure-Track Assistant or Associate Professor of Physics - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Tenure-Track Assistant or Associate Professor of Physics Physics Full Time Permanent - Faculty Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites The Citadel, the Military College of South Carolina, invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-track position in Physics at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor beginning August 2027. We seek a teacher-scholar committed to excellent undergraduate teaching and to developing an active research program that involves undergraduate students. We particularly welcome candidates in experimental or applied physics. One of seven departments in the Swain Family School of Science and Mathematics, the Department of Physics is a collaborative community offering a BS in Applied Physics, a BA in Physics, and minors in applied physics and aerospace science. The department emphasizes excellent teaching, close student mentorship, hands-on learning, undergraduate research, and meaningful faculty engagement in the curriculum. Founded in 1842 and located in historic Charleston, South Carolina, The Citadel is a public, coeducational senior military college dedicated to educating and developing principled leaders. Total enrollment is approximately 3,900 students, including approximately 2,400 members of the South Carolina Corps of Cadets, with additional students enrolled in graduate, evening undergraduate, College Transfer Program, and online offerings. In the 2027 U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings, The Citadel is ranked No. 1 among Regional Universities in the South for the third consecutive year, No. 1 among Public Regional Universities in the South for the 16th consecutive year, and No. 1 among Best Colleges for Veterans in the South for the ninth consecutive year. The Citadel's 12:1 student-to-faculty ratio and average undergraduate class size of approximately 20 support close faculty-student engagement. The Citadel provides internal funding for faculty research, professional development, and travel, and offers competitive benefits. Compensation is competitive and commensurate with credentials and experience. Position Responsibilities Teaching responsibilities will include a mix of introductory physics, courses for physics majors, and general education courses. The standard teaching load is four 3-credit courses per semester or an equivalent combination of lecture and laboratory assignments. We value hands-on and applied approaches that engage students with varied backgrounds and career goals. The successful candidate will maintain an active research program appropriate to a teaching-focused undergraduate institution, producing scholarly work and involving undergraduate students. Startup funding is available, along with internal research grant opportunities. Additional responsibilities include departmental, school, and college service and participation in the department's established outreach activities. Minimum Qualifications Candidates must hold an earned doctorate in physics or a closely related field by the appointment date and demonstrate the potential for excellence in undergraduate teaching, scholarship, and student mentorship. Appointment at the Associate Professor level requires a record of teaching, scholarship, and service commensurate with rank. Application Instructions Applicants should complete the online application and submit the following materials: • A cover letter addressing the candidate's qualifications and interest in the position • An updated curriculum vitae • A statement describing the candidate's approach to undergraduate teaching • A research statement describing a program that incorporates undergraduate students • Contact information for at least three professional references Review of applications will begin December 1, 2026 , and continue until the position is filled. Questions may be directed to Dr. Hank Yochum, Head of the Department of Physics, at 843-953-6953 or hyochum@citadel.edu . Start Your Application First Name (required) b7e9c776 Last Name (required) da5c639c Email (required) c3ff0750 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/w-frank-hipp-distinguished-chair-in-business-administration-accounting-finance-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "W. Frank Hipp Distinguished Chair in Business Administration (Accounting/Finance)",
      "description": "W. Frank Hipp Distinguished Chair in Business Administration (Accounting/Finance) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States W. Frank Hipp Distinguished Chair in Business Administration (Accounting/Finance) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode W. Frank Hipp Distinguished Chair in Business Administration (Accounting/Finance) Accounting and Finance Full Time Permanent - Faculty Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites The Tommy & Victoria Baker School of Business at The Citadel invites applications and nominations for the W. Frank Hipp Distinguished Chair in Business Administration. This position resides in the Department of Accounting and Finance. The W. Frank Hipp Distinguished Chair is an endowed executive-in-residence position established to bring the experience and perspective of a distinguished senior business executive into the educational environment of The Citadel. Consistent with the terms establishing the Chair, the successful candidate will have a demonstrated history of significant leadership responsibilities in a complex organization and will combine substantial executive experience with a strong commitment to educating and mentoring the next generation of business leaders. The governing gift agreement specifically provides for the Chair to be filled by a “distinguished senior executive with a successful history of significant leadership responsibilities in a complex organization” and contemplates a senior executive in residence rather than limiting the position to a senior academician. This is a full-time, nine-month appointment in the Tommy & Victoria Baker School of Business. The successful candidate will receive an initial three-year appointment, with the potential for subsequent one-year extensions following annual review and at the option of The Citadel, consistent with the terms of the endowed Chair. Responsibilities The W. Frank Hipp Distinguished Chair will contribute to the academic and professional mission of the Baker School of Business through teaching, student engagement, service to the School, and engagement with the broader business community. The Chair has traditionally served in the Department of Accounting and Finance. The Chair will: Teach 3 courses per semester. A reduced course load may be considered for a candidate who takes on additional program responsibilities; Teach primarily undergraduate courses, with assignments based upon the candidate's academic preparation, professional qualifications, areas of expertise, and the needs of the School; Serve as a resource to students, faculty, and leadership of the Baker School of Business; Engage with students through mentoring, professional development activities, executive presentations, and other opportunities that bring senior executive experience into the educational environment; Contribute to enhancing the reputation and visibility of The Citadel and the Baker School of Business; Assist in developing and strengthening relationships between the Baker School of Business and the business and professional communities; Participate in appropriate School and College activities where the Chair's executive experience and professional perspective can contribute to the School's mission; and Represent the Baker School of Business appropriately with business leaders, alumni, prospective students, and other external constituencies. Candidates possessing an appropriate terminal degree may also be assigned to teach graduate courses. These responsibilities incorporate the four responsibilities identified in the gift agreement: teaching students, serving as a resource to the School, enhancing The Citadel's image, and assisting in building stronger relationships for the School. Required Qualifications The successful candidate must possess: A minimum of a master's degree in Business or a related field from an appropriately accredited institution; A distinguished record of senior executive leadership with significant leadership responsibilities in a complex organization; Demonstrated professional accomplishments in business, industry, professional practice, entrepreneurship, government, the nonprofit sector, or another organizational setting relevant to business education; The ability to translate substantial professional and executive experience into meaningful educational experiences for undergraduate students; Strong leadership, communication, and interpersonal skills; The ability to develop and maintain relationships with business and community leaders; and A commitment to student development and to the educational mission of The Citadel. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates possessing: A Ph.D. or other appropriate terminal degree in Accounting or Finance; A Master of Accountancy (MAcc), Master of Finance (MFin), or Master of Business Administration (MBA) with a concentration in Accounting or Finance; Significant C-suite or comparable senior executive experience; A record of leadership involving strategic decision-making, organizational change, financial responsibility, and the development of people and organizations; Experience serving on corporate, nonprofit, governmental, or other governing boards; A substantial network within the business and professional community; Experience teaching, mentoring, speaking to, or otherwise working with university students and emerging professionals; and Professional certifications or credentials appropriate to the candidate's field. About the W. Frank Hipp Distinguished Chair The W. Frank Hipp Distinguished Chair in Business Administration was established through the generosity of the Hipp family to advance business education at The Citadel. The governing gift agreement was amended in 2003 to broaden the criteria for the Chair to include a distinguished senior executive with a proven record of significant leadership in a complex organization. The agreement identifies four principal responsibilities for the Chair: teaching undergraduate and graduate students, serving as a resource for the School, enhancing The Citadel's image, and helping build stronger relationships for the School. The position therefore offers an accomplished business leader the opportunity to bring significant real-world leadership and executive experience directly into the classroom while contributing more broadly to student development and the advancement of the Baker School of Business. Appointment and Teaching Expectations The W. Frank Hipp Distinguished Chair is a full-time, nine-month position. Teaching assignments will primarily be at the undergraduate level and will be determined by the candidate's academic preparation, professional qualifications, areas of expertise, and the needs of the Baker School of Business. Candidates possessing a Ph.D. or other appropriate terminal degree may also be assigned to teach graduate courses. The initial appointment will be for three years, with the potential for subsequent one-year extensions following annual review and at the option of The Citadel. Distinctive Features of the Department of Accounting & Finance The Department of Accounting & Finance at The Citadel provides students with rigorous academic preparation and practical experiences that prepare them for success in professional careers and graduate study. Faculty engage closely with students through advising, mentoring, and experiential programs. The department is home to signature initiatives such as the Student-Managed Investment Fund and applied projects that connect students with real-world decision-making. Distinctive Features of the Tommy & Victoria Baker School of Business The Tommy & Victoria Baker School of Business is an AACSB International-accredited institution located on The Citadel's campus in beautiful Charleston, on the coast of South Carolina. Now situated in its own recently completed educational building, the School of Business engages state-of-the-art technology and media resources for innovative, highly effective business education. The School offers multiple undergraduate programs, an undergraduate degree completion program, and an online MBA program. The Baker School of Business serves approximately 1,100 undergraduate and graduate students. The Citadel maintains a heritage of excellence in education, with a strong emphasis on leadership education and development. It has been ranked by U.S. News & World Report for eleven consecutive years as the #1 Public College in the South offering programs leading to a master's degree. It is also named as one of the Ten Most Innovative Schools in the South. The Citadel is home to the South Carolina Corps of Cadets and offers a unique residential undergraduate experience in a military college setting. Graduate students, including MBA students, undertake programs in the nonresidential Citadel Graduate College. The successful candidate will join a well-established team of academic professionals committed to educating and developing innovative leaders of principle to serve a global community. Distinctive Features of The Citadel The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina, is a public senior military college located in Charleston, South Carolina. Founded in 1842, The Citadel has a rich history and educational reputation. Its campus is located on the banks of the Ashley River in downtown Charleston, close to restaurants, shopping, cultural attractions, and other amenities. Approximately 2,300 undergraduate students make up the South Carolina Corps of Cadets. Roughly 30% of cadet graduates earn a military commission. Students can choose from 31 majors, 57 minors, pre-health professions, and pre-law. The 11:1 student-to-faculty ratio provides students with opportunities for close interaction with faculty. Another approximately 1,200 students attend the Citadel Graduate College's evening and online programs. Distinctive Features of Charleston Charleston, South Carolina, provides an extraordinary backdrop for academic and personal life. Consistently ranked among the most beautiful and livable cities in America, Charleston combines historic character with a vibrant economy, culinary distinction, and coastal beauty. Faculty and their families enjoy an exceptional quality of life in a city known for its cultural heritage, innovative spirit, and unmatched lifestyle opportunities. Application Process In addition to the online application, applicants should submit the following materials: A letter of interest describing the applicant's executive leadership experience, interest in the W. Frank Hipp Distinguished Chair, and approach to contributing to the education and professional development of business students; A current curriculum vitae or executive résumé; Evidence of graduate education and relevant professional credentials; and Contact information for at least three professional references. All applications must be submitted electronically through The Citadel Jobs Portal at https://jobs.citadel.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately and will remain open until the position is filled. The position is available beginning January 2027 . The start date is negotiable and may be as early as January 2027, with an expected start no later than August 2027 . Nominations and confidential inquiries are welcomed and may be directed to: Wesley M. Jones, Jr., Ph.D. Chair, Department of Accounting and Finance Tommy and Victoria Baker School of Business The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina 171 Moultrie Street Charleston, SC 29409 843-953-7531 Wes.jones@citadel.edu Start Your Application First Name (required) 04dd94da Last Name (required) 6c8a71d3 Email (required) b29bdcde Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
