    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/tenure-track-assistant-professor-of-leadership-studies-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Leadership Studies",
      "description": "Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Leadership Studies - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Leadership Studies - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Leadership Studies Krause School of Leadership and Ethics Full Time Permanent - Faculty Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites Job Responsibilities: Would you want to join a department whose members are conscientious, dedicated, competent, collegial, and professional, dedicated to teaching students, to engaging in impactful scholarly activity, to supporting the various programs and activities which complement and enhance the college’s educational mission, and to sharing professional expertise with the college and larger communities beyond campus? These expectations of department faculty are traditionally summarized in terms of commitments to teaching, scholarship, and service The Citadel’s Department of Leadership Studies invites applications for a full-time, nine-month, tenure-track faculty member for the position of Assistant Professor of Leadership Studies with a start date of Fall 2027. This new faculty member will join the Krause School of Leadership and Ethics team that opened on July 1, 2026. The Krause School of Leadership and Ethics (KSLE) is The Citadel’s sixth academic school and its most significant academic expansion in recent history. Rooted in the institution’s core mission to develop principled leaders, KSLE formalizes decades of leadership education into a dedicated academic home— bringing together the Department of Leadership Studies, the Krause Center for Leadership Development and Executive and Professional Education under one umbrella. The school was made possible by the generous support of Bill and Gay Krause, whose transformative gift funded renovation of the facility. The mission of the Department of Leadership Studies is to enhance the ability of students from any academic background to perform effectively as principled leaders in their present or future leadership roles. The Leadership Studies Department offers general education leadership courses, an undergraduate minor in leadership studies, a Master of Science leadership as well as graduate certificates in leadership and military leadership at the graduate level. Teaching faculty serve on department and college committees. Minimum Qualifications: Qualified applicants will have a completed a terminal degree at a regionally accredited university in an area well-grounded in leadership theory and related to leadership studies. Preferred Qualifications: Research stream or interest in leadership theory, ethical leadership, nonprofit leadership, or military leadership Understanding and experience with different instructional pedagogies. Expertise teaching graduate students in an online environment. Post-doctoral experience with a demonstrated track record of peer-reviewed publications. Practical leadership experience in professional or community-based leadership roles. Additional Comments: Interested candidates should utilize the official online application website at http://www.citadel.edu/careers/ . In addition to completing the online application, candidates should upload a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a philosophy of teaching statement. All inquiries should be directed to the Human Resources Department at The Citadel. Initial screening of applicants will begin on October 15, 2026 , and continue until the position is filled. The College offers competitive salaries and state government benefits. The Citadel is a landmark institution located on the banks of the Ashley River in Charleston, South Carolina. As an outstanding Senior Military College, The Citadel is committed to educating and developing principled leaders who serve in the military, private, public, and independent sectors. The Citadel is ranked #1 Public College in the South offering up to a master’s degree by U.S. News & World Report . To learn more about The Citadel and the Department of Leadership Studies, visit our website at http://www.citadel.edu/root/leadershipstudies . Benefits of Working at The Citadel Extensive Health Plans Great Retirement Options Tuition Waiver Program Paid Parental Leave Employee Discounts Isle of Palms Beach Club Swain Family Boat Center Community Service Opportunities Mentor/Mentee Program Read more about our benefits, on our HR website About The Citadel College The Citadel, also known as the Military College of South Carolina, is a public senior military college located in Charleston, South Carolina. Founded in 1842, The Citadel has a rich history and educational reputation. With our current location on the banks of the Ashley River in downtown Charleston, you are close to great restaurants, shopping and much more. Ranked #1 Public College in the South for schools with up to a master’s degree, the opportunities are endless. There are about 2,300 undergraduate students who make up the South Carolina Corps of Cadets. Out of the Corps of Cadets, 1 out of 3 graduates earn a military commission. Students can choose from 31 Majors, 57 Minors, pre-health professions, and pre-law (a concentration in political science). The 11:1 student-to-faculty ratio guarantees students a quality education. Another 1,000 students attend the Graduate College, evening, and online programs. Start Your Application First Name (required) 23bc8128 Last Name (required) 661b9318 Email (required) 7ff980b9 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
