    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-electrical-and-computer-engineering-pooled-position-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Electrical and Computer Engineering (pooled position)",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Electrical and Computer Engineering (pooled position) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Adjunct Faculty - Electrical and Computer Engineering (pooled position) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty - Electrical and Computer Engineering (pooled position) Elec and Computer Eng Adjunct Faculty Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites Job Responsibilities: The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina, is seeking applicants for an adjunct faculty position in The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering for the fall and spring semesters. Duties primarily include teaching college undergraduate courses in the electrical and computer engineering curriculum. All adjunct positions are part-time, temporary, and per session appointments. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should have a Master's or Doctorate degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering or a closely related field with a minimum of 18 credit hours in graduate-level related engineering courses. Preferred Qualifications: Previous teaching experience. Please contact Mark McKinney by phone at: 843-953-4897, or by email at: mckinneym@citadel.edu if you have any questions or would like further information. Start Your Application First Name (required) c58e6bad Last Name (required) f6a8df40 Email (required) ca276a3a Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
