    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-tenure-track-counselor-education-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (tenure-track) - Counselor Education",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (tenure-track) - Counselor Education - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Assistant Professor (tenure-track) - Counselor Education - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor (tenure-track) - Counselor Education Zucker Family School of Ed Full Time Permanent - Faculty Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites About The Citadel College: The Citadel, the Military College of South Carolina, is a public senior military college located in Charleston, South Carolina. Founded in 1842, The Citadel has a rich history steeped in tradition and centered on our core values of honor, duty and state and country. The Citadel has been ranked #1 Public College in the South, offering up to a master’s degree, for fourteen consecutive years, and one of the Ten Most Innovative Schools in the South by U.S. News and World Report. The Citadel hosts 2,300 undergraduate students who make up the South Carolina Corps of Cadets with an additional 1,000 students attending the graduate college through evening and online programs. Students can choose from 31 Majors, 57 Minors, pre-health professions, and pre-law (a concentration in political science) with an 11:1 student-to-faculty ratio guaranteeing students a quality education. The Citadel is a senior military college, and our graduate programs enroll civilian students taught by faculty who are career educators. If you are looking for a place where your teaching load is real, your students are close at hand, and your colleagues know P-12 schools from the inside, this is that place. Charleston is a good place to live while you do it. Along with a great environment for students and faculty, The Citadel is located on the banks of the Ashley River in downtown Charleston, where you will be close to great restaurants, shopping and all of the art, entertainment and culture that can only be found in historic Charleston. Position Summary The Zucker Family School of Education at The Citadel invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Counselor Education with a focus on school counseling, beginning August 2027. The ideal candidate will have experience as a school counselor and will teach graduate school counseling courses on a 3-3 load, supervise students through their field experiences, and advise and mentor students from admission through licensure. The successful applicant will be expected to build a research agenda that leads to peer-reviewed publications and/or securing external funding. Candidates will help shape curriculum and program development, contribute to our CACREP accreditation work, partner with local P-12 districts and community agencies, and stay active in the professional life of the field. Service on school, college, and professional committees is also an expectation. The ideal candidate will hold a doctorate in Counselor Education from a CACREP-accredited institution by August 2027 and who has a record of success as a certified professional school counselor. Candidates should bring demonstrated multicultural competence in both counseling and teaching, a clear plan for scholarship, and teaching skills that work in face-to-face and online settings. Preference will be given to candidates that demonstrate innovative uses of technology as an instructional tool, and willingness to work as a team member in implementing and reviewing CACREP standards. Special Instructions to Applicants: To Apply, please complete the online application and in addition, please attach the following: Letter of interest Curriculum vitae Teaching statement and evidence of teaching quality Unofficial transcripts Names, phone numbers and emails for three references with your application Review of candidates will begin October 15, 2026 , and continue until the position has been filled. Start Your Application First Name (required) e33df16c Last Name (required) 481fc439 Email (required) 7111e7f6 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-department-of-psychology-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Department of Psychology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Department of Psychology - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Assistant Professor - Department of Psychology - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor - Department of Psychology Psychology Full Time Permanent - Faculty 70,000 Add to favorites View favorites The Department of Psychology at The Citadel invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Psychology (specialization is open, preference given to Experimental Psychology) to begin in August 2027. The successful candidate is expected to actively engage undergraduate students in their research program. Located in historic Charleston, South Carolina, The Citadel has been ranked for the past 8 years (by U.S. News and World Report ) as the top public college in the South among master’s-granting institutions. The Citadel’s Psychology Department has long been recognized for supporting and advancing diversity, equity, and inclusion. Candidates that can speak to and add to this mission are strongly encouraged to apply. Position Responsibilities The position will primarily entail teaching undergraduate courses based on the candidate’s specialization and also will include teaching Research Methods at the graduate level for Master’s students enrolled in the School Psychology and Clinical Counseling programs. Preference will be given to candidates who can teach core courses in the undergraduate program (Introduction to Psychological Science, Psychological Statistics, Research Design/Experimental Psychology), along with elective courses in the candidate’s area of specialization (e.g., Social Psychology, Sports Psychology, Health Psychology, Neuroscience, etc.). Other position-related responsibilities include: maintaining an active and productive research program (specific areas of expertise are open), supervising undergraduate student research, engaging in service initiatives across the program, department, college, community, and/or professional levels, contributing to program-related activities as needed, and serving as a positive role model for undergraduate and graduate students. Required Qualifications Minimum requirements include a doctorate in an experimental area of psychology or related discipline (ABD candidates will be considered), as well as demonstrated research potential and the willingness to maintain a productive research program that incorporates undergraduate students. Preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate evidence of teaching experience and instructional effectiveness at the post-secondary level. The Department of Psychology (with 11 full-time faculty) has approximately 75 undergraduate majors; additionally, we have approximately 100 graduate students between the two programs housed within the Department of Psychology – School Psychology and Clinical Counseling, both accredited (by NASP and MPCAC, respectively). The Citadel is a co-educational military college that provides a unique undergraduate learning environment complemented by a non-military Citadel Graduate College. The Citadel Foundation provides generous support for faculty research and professional travel. The campus is located on the banks of the Ashley River on the Charleston peninsula, where the mild winters, nearby beaches, rich cultural activities, and award-winning culinary options combine to create a vibrant place to live. Additionally, the nearby Medical University of South Carolina, Ralph H Johnson VA Hospital, and local school districts offer opportunities for collaboration and research. The Citadel is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and does not discriminate against any individual, or group of individuals, on the basis of age, color, race, disability, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, religion, pregnancy, national origin, genetic information or veteran's status in its employment practices. The Citadel has a culturally diverse faculty and staff committed to working in a multicultural environment. We encourage applications from minorities, females, individuals with disabilities and veterans. Salary and Compensation Starting salary is commensurate with qualifications and credentials. The anticipated starting date is mid-August 2027. This is a nine-month tenure-track position, although summer teaching opportunities may be available. Candidates should apply online at www.jobs.sc.gov . Please attach the following: curriculum vitae; cover letter that addresses teaching interests and philosophy, research interests, and general suitability for the position; relevant reprints/preprints (which may be hyperlinked within vitae or cover letter if preferred); and at least three letters of reference. Questions may be directed to Audrey Parrish at aparrish@citadel.edu . Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. To find out more about The Citadel and life in Charleston, check out this video, https://vimeo.com/749600455/d65c9eabe2 ! Review of candidates will begin November 2, 2026, and continue until the position has been filled. Start Your Application First Name (required) 96e7d9ec Last Name (required) 1f087098 Email (required) 42ca8205 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/associate-professor-of-stem-education-and-director-of-the-anita-zucker-institute-for-entrepreneurial-educational-leadership-at-the-stem-center-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Professor of STEM Education and Director of the Anita Zucker Institute for Entrepreneurial Educational Leadership at the STEM Center",
      "description": "Associate Professor of STEM Education and Director of the Anita Zucker Institute for Entrepreneurial Educational Leadership at the STEM Center - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Associate Professor of STEM Education and Director of the Anita Zucker Institute for Entrepreneurial Educational Leadership at the STEM Center - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Associate Professor of STEM Education and Director of the Anita Zucker Institute for Entrepreneurial Educational Leadership at the STEM Center Zucker Family School of Ed Full Time Permanent - Faculty Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites About The Citadel College: The Citadel, the Military College of South Carolina, is a public senior military college located in Charleston, South Carolina. Founded in 1842, The Citadel has a rich history steeped in tradition and centered on our core values of honor, duty and state and country. The Citadel has been ranked #1 Public College in the South, offering up to a master’s degree, for fourteen consecutive years, and one of the Ten Most Innovative Schools in the South by U.S. News and World Report. The Citadel hosts 2,300 undergraduate students who make up the South Carolina Corps of Cadets with an additional 1,000 students attending the graduate college through evening and online programs. Students can choose from 31 Majors, 57 Minors, pre-health professions, and pre-law (a concentration in political science) with an 11:1 student-to-faculty ratio guaranteeing students a quality education. Along with a great environment for students and faculty, The Citadel is located on the banks of the Ashley River in downtown Charleston, where you will be close to great restaurants, shopping and all of the art, entertainment and culture that can only be found in historic Charleston. Position Summary The Citadel’s Zucker Family School of Education invites applications for a tenure-track Associate Professor of Education position specializing in STEM Teacher Education. Special consideration will be given to applicants with computer science education and a STEM education Discipline (e.g., science education or mathematics education) background, beginning August 2027. We seek candidates with a commitment to working collaboratively with faculty and staff to prepared and to support K-12 STEM teacher candidates that integrate computational thinking/computer science/disruptive technologies into their content area classrooms in South Carolina. Candidates contributing to our school’s mission are encouraged to identify their experiences in their cover letter. This position also comes with a directorship for the Anita Zucker Institute for Entrepreneurial Educational Leadership in the STEM Center. The director will manage daily operations, scheduling, relationship building, and student support. Candidates for this position will show strong leadership, budgeting, verbal and written communication, and problem-solving skills. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and graduate STEM education and computer science education programs. Candidates must demonstrate a record of, or potential for, scholarly activity, including peer-reviewed publications, presentations, and securing external grant funding. Additional responsibilities include student mentorship through advising and collaborative undergraduate research and contributions to the life of the school, college, and profession. Minimum Required Education and Experience An earned doctorate from an accredited university in teacher education, curriculum and instruction, computer science education, teaching and learning, or related field; an established record of research work in STEM teacher education; demonstrated success as a 6-12 teacher and/or 6-12 certified professional; ability to collaborate with local P-12 school districts; and commitment to preparing professional educators to work in a variety of school environments. Preferred Qualifications: Teaching skills that employ a variety of instructional strategies in both face-to-face and online environments. At least 3 years of experience teaching in a public school Special Instructions to Applicants: To Apply: Please attach with your online application the following: (1) letter of interest, (2) curriculum vitae, (3) a teaching statement and evidence of teaching quality (4) names, phone numbers and emails for three references and (4) unofficial transcripts with your application. Review of candidates will begin October 15, 2027, and continue until the position has been filled. Start Your Application First Name (required) 169a4e5a Last Name (required) fa537dde Email (required) 1d003c46 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/dean-school-of-engineering-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Dean - School of Engineering",
      "description": "Dean - School of Engineering - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Dean - School of Engineering - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Dean - School of Engineering Provost and Dean of College Full Time Permanent - Faculty Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites Dean, School of Engineering, The Citadel The Citadel invites nominations and applications for the position of Dean of the School of Engineering, who also holds the Col. Louis S. Le Tellier Chair in Engineering. Candidates must hold an earned doctorate and demonstrate a strong commitment to advancing education and scholarship at a student-centered college. Founded in 1842, The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina, is a coeducational, state-assisted college dedicated to excellence in educating principled leaders. Total enrollment is approximately 3,900 students, including approximately 2,400 members of the South Carolina Corps of Cadets and students enrolled in graduate, evening undergraduate, College Transfer Program (CTP), and online offerings. In the latest U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings, The Citadel is ranked No. 1 among Regional Universities in the South for the second consecutive year, No. 1 among Public Regional Universities in the South for the 15th consecutive year, and No. 1 among Best Colleges for Veterans in the South for the eighth consecutive year. The Citadel also ranks No. 14 nationally for Best Undergraduate Engineering Programs at institutions where a doctorate is not offered. The nationally ranked School of Engineering offers five ABET-accredited undergraduate engineering programs: Civil and Environmental Engineering, Computer Engineering, Construction Engineering, Electrical Engineering, and Mechanical Engineering. The School also offers four Master of Science degree programs in Civil Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, and Project Management (GAC accredited). These programs are supported by 33 full-time faculty members and seven staff members, with 21 adjunct faculty members providing additional instructional support. The School enrolls 665 students: 565 undergraduates across its five bachelor's degree programs, including 80 students in the College Transfer Program, and 100 graduate students across its four Master of Science degree programs. This is an exciting period for the School of Engineering, with construction beginning on a 106,000-square-foot facility scheduled to open in 2029. The Dean oversees the School's daily operations and coordinates, supports, and advances a broad range of educational and scholarly activities through collaborative, empowering, and relationship-centered leadership. The Citadel seeks a proven leader with a distinguished academic record and substantial administrative and leadership experience. The Dean will also lead the School's fundraising and development efforts in close partnership with The Citadel Foundation staff and the School's Advisory Board. The successful candidate must work effectively and collaboratively with faculty across all of the College's academic units and remain committed to excellent teaching, high-quality scholarly activity, and professional development in a student-centered environment. Required qualifications: An earned doctorate in a discipline represented in the School or in a closely related field. Demonstrated excellence in the scholarship of teaching and learning, classroom instruction, research, and scholarly work sufficient to qualify for appointment as a tenured full professor in one of The Citadel's academic departments. A record of progressively responsible and effective administrative experience in higher education, including planning, resource development, budgeting, and faculty development. Demonstrated commitment to excellence in recruiting, retaining, and developing students and faculty. Evidence of excellent communication, listening, and interpersonal skills. Demonstrated ability to build strong collaborations and relationships with internal and external constituencies. A proven record of effectively administering ABET accreditation and assessment processes. A proven ability to work effectively and collaboratively with faculty through shared governance, together with a commitment to educational excellence and meaningful service consistent with The Citadel's mission and core values. Preferred qualifications: Demonstrated success as an outstanding fundraiser with college alumni and friends, industry, and government. Demonstrated ability to secure external resources through grants, contracts, and gifts. Professional registration. A proven record of effectively administering GAC accreditation and assessment processes. Demonstrated ability to develop or increase enrollment in graduate or online programs. Demonstrated involvement in engineering education through ASEE, IEEE, ASME, ASCE, or comparable professional organizations. Compensation is competitive and commensurate with credentials and experience. Applications should include a statement of educational philosophy and leadership style, a curriculum vitae, and the names, email addresses, and telephone numbers of at least three references. Review of applications will begin September 30, 2026 , and continue until an appointment is made. Questions regarding this position may be directed to Dr. Darin Zimmerman, Dean of the Swain Family School of Science and Mathematics and Chair of the Search Committee. Start Your Application First Name (required) 8315c261 Last Name (required) 541355cd Email (required) 1c3712ef Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/provost-and-dean-of-the-college-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Provost and Dean of the College",
      "description": "Provost and Dean of the College - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Provost and Dean of the College - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Provost and Dean of the College Provost and Dean of College Full Time Permanent - Faculty Full Time Permanent - Staff Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites PROVOST AND DEAN OF THE COLLEGE The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina, seeks an accomplished academic leader to serve as Provost and Dean of the College. Reporting to the President, the Provost serves as the College's Chief Academic Officer, directing the Deans of the College's Schools and collaborating with the Commandant's office to align the academic and military components of a Citadel education. The Provost will also collaborate with the college’s other Vice Presidents as part of the President’s senior leadership team. Founded in 1842, The Citadel is one of the nation's senior military colleges, located on a 300-acre campus in Charleston, South Carolina. The College is home to the South Carolina Corps of Cadets, numbering approximately 2,300 students, as well as The Citadel Graduate College, which serves close to 1,000 students through evening, online, and graduate programs. The Citadel has been named the No. 1 public regional university in the South by U.S. News & World Report for 15 consecutive years, and the No. 1 public college for veterans in the South for eight years. Gen. Frank McKenzie, a 1979 Citadel graduate, began his tenure as the College's 21st President in July of this year. Academic programs are organized across the Tommy and Victoria Baker School of Business, the School of Engineering, the School of Humanities and Social Sciences, the Swain Family School of Science and Mathematics, the Zucker Family School of Education, and the Krause School for Leadership and Ethics, along with The Citadel Graduate College. The College maintains an 11:1 student-to-faculty ratio, and nearly all faculty hold a doctorate or the highest degree in their field. The successful candidate will bring a record of academic leadership, including experience with faculty affairs, curriculum, and accreditation, along with the ability to lead within a structured, values-driven military campus culture. Qualified candidates must hold an earned doctorate or terminal degree, possess scholarly credentials appropriate for a tenured appointment, and demonstrate a successful record of senior academic leadership at the dean level or higher. Experience with both a traditional undergraduate program and adult, graduate, or online education is preferred. Military experience is not necessary, but the Provost will wear a uniform and will hold the grade of Brigadier General in the South Carolina Militia (SCM). Applications, nominations, and inquiries should be directed to the search firm contact listed below. Review of candidates will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Interested parties are encouraged to submit their materials to our consultant at the address below by November 1, 2026, for full consideration. Application materials must include a current CV and letter of interest. The Citadel Provost and Dean of the College Search Funk Associates 2911 Turtle Creek Boulevard, Suite 300 Dallas, Texas 75219 Email: Krisha.Creal@funkassociates.com Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/tenure-track-assistant-associate-or-full-professor-of-finance-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of Finance",
      "description": "Tenure-Track Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of Finance - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Tenure-Track Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of Finance - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Tenure-Track Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of Finance Accounting and Finance Full Time Permanent - Faculty Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites Tenure-Track Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of Finance The Tommy and Victoria Baker School of Business at The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina, invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position in Finance at the Assistant, Associate or Full Professor level, beginning Fall 2027. Position Opportunities The Baker School of Business seeks outstanding teacher-scholars in finance. Candidates with expertise in investments, portfolio management, and security analysis will have the opportunity to engage students directly in managing the Student-Managed Investment Fund (SMIF), a $2.5 million portfolio that provides hands-on experience in professional asset management. Candidates with interests in financial planning, wealth management, and financial management will contribute to curriculum development aligned with the CFA Institute and CFP Board, preparing students for leadership roles in personal financial planning, corporate finance, and related fields. Qualifications Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in Finance from an AACSB-accredited institution (ABD considered for assistant professors if completion will occur prior to employment). Candidates should demonstrate potential for excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. Preferred qualifications include CFA or CFP credentials, relevant professional experience, and a record of or strong potential for publishing in peer-reviewed journals. Distinctive Features of the Department of Accounting & Finance The Department of Accounting & Finance at The Citadel provides students with rigorous academic preparation and practical experiences that prepare them for success in professional careers and graduate study. Faculty engage closely with students through advising, mentoring, and experiential programs. The department is home to signature initiatives such as the Student-Managed Investment Fund and applied projects that connect students with real-world decision-making. Distinctive Features of the Baker School of Business The Tommy & Victoria Baker School of Business is an AACSB International-accredited institution located on The Citadel’s campus in beautiful Charleston, on the coast of South Carolina. Now situated in its own recently completed educational building, the School of Business engages state-of-the-art technology and media resources for innovative, highly effective business education. The School offers multiple undergraduate programs, an undergraduate degree completion program, and an online MBA program. The Baker School of Business serves approximately 1,100 undergraduate and graduate students. The Citadel maintains a heritage of excellence in education, with a strong emphasis on leadership education and development. It has been ranked by U.S. News and World Report for eleven consecutive years as the #1 Public College in the South, offering programs leading to a master’s degree. It is also named as one of the Ten Most Innovative Schools in the South. The Citadel is the home of the South Carolina Corps of Cadets and offers a unique, residential undergraduate experience in a military college setting. Graduate students, including MBA students, undertake programs in the nonresidential Citadel Graduate College. You would join us as an integral member of a well-established team of academic professionals who are committed to educating and developing innovative leaders of principle to serve a global community. The Citadel is fully EEO compliant . Distinctive Features of The Citadel The Citadel: The Military College of South Carolina is a public senior military college located in Charleston, South Carolina. Founded in 1842, The Citadel has a rich history and educational reputation. With our current location on the banks of the Ashley River in downtown Charleston, you are close to great restaurants, shopping and much more. Approximately 2,300 undergraduate students make up the South Carolina Corps of Cadets. Roughly 30% of our cadet graduates earn a military commission. Students can choose from 31 Majors, 57 Minors, pre-health professions, and pre-law (a concentration in political science). The 11:1 student-to-faculty ratio ensures students receive a high-quality education. Another 1,200 students attend the Citadel Graduate College’s evening and online programs. Distinctive Features of Charleston Charleston, South Carolina, provides an extraordinary backdrop for academic and personal life. Consistently ranked among the most beautiful and livable cities in America, Charleston combines historic character with a vibrant economy, culinary distinction, and coastal beauty. Faculty and their families enjoy an exceptional quality of life in a city known for its cultural heritage, innovative spirit, and unmatched lifestyle opportunities. Application Instructions Dr. Wesley Jones, Search Committee Chair and Department Chair of Accounting & Finance, will be attending the Financial Management Association (FMA) Annual Meeting in October. Candidates attending the conference are encouraged to email him at jonesw1@citadel.edu to arrange a meeting during the event. Candidates unable to attend may also email to request a Zoom meeting. Applicants should submit the following: - Cover letter addressing qualifications and interest in the position - Curriculum vitae - Statement of teaching philosophy - Statement of research interests and scholarly agenda - Evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g., student evaluations, sample syllabi) - Contact information for three professional references Priority review of applications will begin on August 20, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Materials should be submitted electronically to https://jobs.citadel.edu/ Start Your Application First Name (required) 30e672a0 Last Name (required) fec1e830 Email (required) b8c35e2c Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/department-head-and-associate-professor-professor-of-accounting-or-finance-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Department Head and Associate Professor/Professor of Accounting or Finance",
      "description": "Department Head and Associate Professor/Professor of Accounting or Finance - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Department Head and Associate Professor/Professor of Accounting or Finance - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Department Head and Associate Professor/Professor of Accounting or Finance Accounting and Finance Full Time Permanent - Faculty Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites Department Head and Associate Professor/Professor, Department of Accounting & Finance Tommy & Victoria Baker School of Business The Citadel – Charleston, South Carolina The Tommy & Victoria Baker School of Business at The Citadel invites applications and nominations for the position of Department Head and Associate Professor/Professor in the Department of Accounting & Finance. This is an outstanding opportunity to lead a thriving undergraduate department of approximately 300 students and 10 full-time faculty members within an AACSB-accredited business school committed to academic excellence, principled leadership, and continuous improvement. The successful candidate will serve as Department Head while holding a faculty appointment in either Accounting or Finance at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor , commensurate with qualifications and experience. The Department Head reports directly to the Associate Dean of the Tommy & Victoria Baker School of Business. The Opportunity The Department of Accounting & Finance seeks a collaborative, visionary, and student-centered academic leader who will build upon a strong foundation while helping shape the department's future. The successful candidate will join a collegial faculty dedicated to outstanding teaching, meaningful scholarship and professional engagement, and preparing graduates for successful careers in accounting, finance, and related professions. Working collaboratively with faculty, the Associate Dean, and other university leaders, the Department Head will strengthen academic programs, recruit and mentor outstanding faculty, enhance student engagement and career readiness, foster innovation in teaching and learning, and cultivate relationships with alumni, employers, and the regional business community. This position offers the opportunity to lead through collaboration, develop both people and programs, and advance a department that values excellence, integrity, continuous improvement, and shared governance. About the Department The Department of Accounting & Finance offers Bachelor of Science in Business Administration degree programs in Accounting and Finance and supports the Tommy & Victoria Baker School of Business through teaching in the Master of Business Administration program. The department serves approximately 300 undergraduate students and consists of 10 full-time faculty members , supported by a talented group of adjunct faculty who contribute significant academic and professional expertise. As part of an AACSB-accredited business school, the department is committed to academic excellence, ethical leadership, continuous improvement, and student success. Faculty are recognized for their commitment to outstanding teaching, close faculty-student engagement, scholarly and professional achievement, and service to the institution and profession. Students benefit from experiential learning opportunities including the Student-Managed Investment Fund, the Bastin Financial Leadership Laboratory featuring Bloomberg technology, internships, undergraduate research, and meaningful interaction with faculty mentors and business professionals. Located in historic Charleston, South Carolina, The Citadel is one of the nation's most distinctive public institutions of higher education. The University's mission is to educate and develop principled leaders through a rigorous academic experience grounded in integrity, leadership, and service. Required Qualifications Applicants must possess: An earned doctorate in Accounting or Finance from an accredited institution. Qualifications for appointment as a tenured Associate Professor or Professor . A distinguished record of excellence in teaching, scholarly or professional engagement, and service appropriate to the applicant's academic rank. Demonstrated academic leadership with evidence of sound judgment, collaboration, consensus building, and successful faculty development. Excellent interpersonal, organizational, written, and oral communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Preference will be given to candidates with: Successful experience as a department chair, department head, program director, associate dean, or in another significant academic leadership role. Experience with AACSB accreditation, faculty qualifications, assurance of learning, strategic planning, and continuous improvement. Experience with faculty recruitment, mentoring, evaluation, budgeting, and resource management. Demonstrated success in developing partnerships with alumni, employers, professional organizations, and community stakeholders. A leadership philosophy characterized by collaboration, transparency, integrity, accountability, innovation, and student success. Responsibilities The Department Head provides academic and administrative leadership for the Department of Accounting & Finance and works collaboratively with the Associate Dean, faculty, staff, students, alumni, and external stakeholders to advance the department's mission and strategic priorities. Responsibilities include: Providing strategic leadership and articulating a shared vision for the department's continued success. Recruiting, mentoring, developing, supporting, and evaluating faculty and staff. Promoting excellence in teaching, scholarly and professional engagement, and service. Leading curriculum development, academic assessment, program review, and continuous improvement initiatives. Providing departmental leadership for AACSB accreditation, including faculty qualifications, assurance of learning, and continuous improvement. Managing departmental budgets, faculty workload assignments, course scheduling, and departmental resources. Supporting innovation in curriculum, pedagogy, experiential learning, and student engagement. Promoting student recruitment, retention, mentoring, and career preparation. Building productive relationships with alumni, employers, advisory board members, and the business community. Representing the department within the School of Business, throughout the University, and with external constituents. Teaching courses appropriate to the successful candidate's discipline while maintaining faculty qualifications consistent with AACSB standards. The Department Head teaches a reduced load of two courses per semester , allowing continued engagement in teaching, scholarship or professional engagement, and service while providing effective academic and administrative leadership. Administrative support is provided through a shared administrative assistant serving the School's three academic departments. Application Process Applicants should submit all required application materials electronically through The Citadel's employment website at jobs.citadel.edu . Review of applications will begin at the start of the 2026–2027 academic year (approximately August 15, 2026) and will continue until the position is filled. Application materials should include: A letter of interest addressing the candidate's qualifications for the position and leadership philosophy. A current curriculum vitae. A statement of leadership philosophy Contact information for at least three professional references. Recruiting at Professional Meetings Representatives of the Department of Accounting & Finance will be available to meet with prospective applicants during the Financial Management Association (FMA) Annual Meeting and the American Accounting Association (AAA) Annual Meeting . Prospective candidates who plan to attend either conference and would like to discuss the Department Head opportunity or the accompanying Accounting and Finance faculty positions are encouraged to contact Wesley M. Jones, Jr., Department Head , at jonesw1@citadel.edu to arrange a convenient meeting. Start Your Application First Name (required) 4dc49d82 Last Name (required) b2fe22d7 Email (required) 4d218fc9 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-full-professor-of-accounting-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Accounting",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Accounting - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Accounting - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Accounting Accounting and Finance Full Time Permanent - Faculty Add to favorites View favorites Tenure-Track Assistant, Associate or Full Professor of Accounting The Tommy and Victoria Baker School of Business at The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina, invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position in Accounting at the Assistant, Associate or Professor level, beginning Fall 2027. Position Responsibilities The successful candidate will: Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in accounting. Maintain Scholarly Academic (SA) status through ongoing high-quality peer-reviewed publications and other scholarly activities, in accordance with Baker School of Business criteria. Advise and mentor accounting majors, supporting their academic, professional, and ethical development. Actively promote the accounting program both within the institution and externally through professional engagement. Participate in normal service activities, including departmental and school-level committee work. Qualifications Minimum: An earned doctorate in Accounting from an AACSB-accredited (or equivalent) institution (ABD candidates will be considered for the assistant professor level if the dissertation defense is expected before employment begins). Demonstrated potential for excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. Preferred: Active professional licensure (e.g., CPA, CMA). Professional experience in accounting or a related field. A record of or potential for publishing in high-quality peer-reviewed academic journals. The Citadel’s Tommy & Victoria Baker School of Business The Tommy & Victoria Baker School of Business is an AACSB International-accredited institution located on The Citadel’s campus in beautiful Charleston, on the coast of South Carolina. Now situated in its own recently completed educational building, the School of Business engages state-of-the-art technology and media resources for innovative, highly effective business education. The School offers multiple undergraduate programs, an undergraduate degree completion program, and an online MBA program. The Baker School of Business serves approximately 1,100 undergraduate and graduate students. The Citadel maintains a heritage of excellence in education, with a strong emphasis on leadership education and development. It has been ranked by U.S. News and World Report for eleven consecutive years as the #1 Public College in the South, offering programs leading to a master’s degree. It is also named as one of the Ten Most Innovative Schools in the South. The Citadel is the home of the South Carolina Corps of Cadets and offers a unique, residential undergraduate experience in a military college setting. Graduate students, including MBA students, undertake programs in the nonresidential Citadel Graduate College. You would join us as an integral member of a well-established team of academic professionals who are committed to educating and developing innovative leaders of principle to serve a global community. About The Citadel The Citadel: The Military College of South Carolina is a public senior military college located in Charleston, South Carolina. Founded in 1842, The Citadel has a rich history and educational reputation. With our current location on the banks of the Ashley River in downtown Charleston, you are close to great restaurants, shopping and much more. Approximately 2,300 undergraduate students make up the South Carolina Corps of Cadets. Roughly 30% of our cadet graduates earn a military commission. Students can choose from 31 Majors, 57 Minors, pre-health professions, and pre-law (a concentration in political science). The 11:1 student-to-faculty ratio ensures students receive a high-quality education. Another 1,200 students attend the Citadel Graduate College’s evening and online programs. Benefits of Working at The Citadel Extensive Health Plans Great Retirement Options Tuition Exchange Program for Dependents Paid Parental Leave Isle of Palms Beach Club Swain Family Boat Center Community Service Opportunities Read more about our benefits on our HR website Application Instructions Dr. Wesley Jones, Department Head for Accounting and Finance, will be attending the American Accounting Association (AAA) Annual Meeting in August. Candidates attending the conference are encouraged to email him at jonesw1@citadel.edu to arrange a meeting during the event. Candidates unable to attend may also email to request a Zoom meeting. Applicants should submit the following: - Cover letter addressing qualifications and interest in the position - Curriculum vitae - Statement of teaching philosophy - Statement of research interests and scholarly agenda - Evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g., student evaluations, sample syllabi) - Contact information for three professional references Priority review of applications will begin on August 20, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Materials should be submitted electronically to https://jobs.citadel.edu/ Why Charleston? Located in one of America’s most beautiful and livable cities, Charleston, South Carolina offers a rich blend of history, culture, culinary excellence, and coastal charm. The city consistently ranks among the best in the U.S. for quality of life, and its vibrant economy, temperate climate, and recreational opportunities make it an ideal location for faculty and families alike. Start Your Application First Name (required) a175d954 Last Name (required) eacfc769 Email (required) 4aca9bc8 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
