    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-psychology-pooled-positions-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Psychology (pooled positions)",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Psychology (pooled positions) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Adjunct Faculty - Psychology (pooled positions) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty - Psychology (pooled positions) Psychology Adjunct Faculty Add to favorites View favorites The Department of Psychology at The Citadel, the Military College of South Carolina, is seeking applications for adjunct faculty positions. Courses taught will be at both the graduate and undergraduate level. Minimum Qualifications: Adjunct positions at the graduate level require a doctoral degree. A master's degree is required to teach at the undergraduate level. Courses taught will vary from semester to semester based on departmental needs. Preference will be given to applicants who have previous effective teaching experience. If you have specific questions please contract, Dr. Chip Taylor at 843-953-5320 or taylorc1@citadel.edu . *Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until positions are filled.* About The Citadel College: The Citadel, the Military College of South Carolina, is a public senior military college located in Charleston, South Carolina. Founded in 1842, The Citadel has a rich history and educational reputation. With our current location on the banks of the Ashley River in downtown Charleston, you are close to great restaurants, shopping and much more. There are about 2,300 undergraduate students who make up the South Carolina Corps of Cadets. Out of the Corps of Cadets, 1 out of 3 graduates earn a military commission. Students can choose from 31 Majors, 57 Minors, pre-health professions, and pre-law (a concentration in political science). The 11:1 student-to-faculty ratio guarantees students a quality education. Another 1,000 students attend the Graduate College, evening and online programs. Start Your Application First Name (required) dc479d07 Last Name (required) 74c64285 Email (required) cd1227ab Apply Pl