    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-modern-languages-german-pooled-position-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Modern Languages - German (pooled position)",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Modern Languages - German (pooled position) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Adjunct Faculty - Modern Languages - German (pooled position) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty - Modern Languages - German (pooled position) Modern Language Adjunct Faculty Add to favorites View favorites The Citadel’s German Program is seeking an Adjunct Instructor to teach one course this fall, starting August 2026, with opportunities for continued teaching beyond the fall semester. Subject to experience and availability, teaching assignment may be for beginning through intermediate language and cultural instruction. All of our courses are taught in person in German and are scheduled weekdays between the hours of 8 a.m. and 2 p.m. Either a TR or MWF schedule can be arranged. Minimum Qualifications: The position requires near native fluency in both English and German and a master’s degree in German, or a master’s degree in another subject with 18 hours of graduate-level study in German or equivalent. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with undergraduate teaching preferred. Interested applicants should start by sending a brief letter of application and a CV to: Dr. Amy Emm (emma1@citadel.edu), Department of Modern Languages, Literatures, and Cultures, The Citadel. About The Citadel College: The Citadel, the Military College of South Carolina, is a public senior military college located in Charleston, South Carolina. Founded in 1842, The Citadel has a rich history and educational reputation. With our current location on the banks of the Ashley River in downtown Charleston, you are close to great restaurants, shopping and much more. Ranked #1 Public College in the South (U.S. News & World Report, 2022) for schools with up to a master’s degree, the opportunities are endless. There are about 2,300 undergraduate students who make up the South Carolina Corps of Cadets. Out of the Corps of Cadets, 1 out of 3