    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-department-of-mechanical-engineering-pooled-positions-charleston-south-carolina-united-states-7fb30c5c-eaf1-4f5c-8f02-bea0db831f3d": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Department of Mechanical Engineering (pooled positions)",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Department of Mechanical Engineering (pooled positions) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Adjunct Faculty - Department of Mechanical Engineering (pooled positions) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty - Department of Mechanical Engineering (pooled positions) Mechanical Engineering Adjunct Faculty Add to favorites View favorites Job Responsibilities: The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina is seeking applicants for an adjunct faculty position in The Department of Mechanical Engineering for the fall and spring semesters. Duties primarily include teaching college undergraduate courses in the mechanical engineering curriculum. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should have a Master's or Doctorate degree in Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, or a closely related field; with a minimum of 18 credit hours in graduate-level engineering courses. Preferred Qualifications: Previous teaching experience. Start Your Application First Name (required) a36a4dfb Last Name (required) 2558c5a2 Email (required) 76cdd99e Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is current