    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-modern-languages-spanish-pooled-position-charleston-south-carolina-united-states-cf30acc3-65be-48e7-9c81-689b9a407c3b": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Modern Languages - Spanish (pooled position)",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Modern Languages - Spanish (pooled position) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Adjunct Faculty - Modern Languages - Spanish (pooled position) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty - Modern Languages - Spanish (pooled position) Modern Language Adjunct Faculty Add to favorites View favorites The Department of Languages, Literatures & Cultures at The Citadel seeks applicants for adjunct faculty positions in Spanish. The Citadel’s goal is to build long-term relationships with high-quality part-time faculty members who are committed to developing principled, well-rounded leaders who appreciate the value of being culturally and linguistically proficient in world languages other than their own. Adjunct professors will teach basic and intermediate language courses. This job posting is not for a specific assignment or for a full-time faculty position, but rather for a pool of candidates who may be considered. Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree from an accredited institution in Spanish or a Master's degree in a different discipline with 18 graduate level credits in Spanish is required. Be able to teach in-person classes, on campus in Charleston, SC. Evidence of previous effective teaching experience is required. Complete Citadel instructor training and follow rules and regulations set by The Citadel Center for Excellence and Innovation in Teaching, Learning, and Distance Education (CEITL&DE). Interview in the target language prior to employment. Preference is given to applicants who meet Scholarly Academic, Practice Academic, Scholarly Practitioner, or Instructional Practitioner and are native-like proficient in the language they desire to teach. Official transcripts indicating education level, interview in the target language, and a background check are required prior to employment. Interested applicants should start by sending a brief letter of application and a CV to: Dr. Vicente Gomis-Izquierdo (vgmomisiz@citadel.edu), Department of Modern Languages, Literatures, and Cultures. About The Citadel College The Citadel, also known as the Military College of South Carolina, is a public senior military college located in Charleston, South Carolina. Founded in 1842, The Citadel has a rich history and educational reputation. With our current location on the banks of the Ashley River in downtown Charleston, you are close to great restaurants, shopping and much more. Ranked #1 Public College in the South (U.S. News & World Report) for schools with up to a master’s degree, the opportunities are endless. There are about 2,300 undergraduate students who make up the South Carolina Corps of Cadets. Out of the Corps of Cadets, 1 out of 3 graduates earn a military commission. Students can choose from 31 Majors, 57 Minors, pre-health professions, and pre-law (a concentration in political science). The 11:1 student-to-faculty ratio guarantees students a quality education. Another 1,000 students attend the Graduate College, evening and online programs. Start Your Application First Name (required) 7014f7ee Last Name (required) 44c290d7 Email (required) 472d24ef Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
