    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-baker-school-of-business-management-and-entrepreneurship-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Baker School of Business - Management and Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Baker School of Business - Management and Entrepreneurship - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Adjunct Faculty - Baker School of Business - Management and Entrepreneurship - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty - Baker School of Business - Management and Entrepreneurship Mgmt and Entrepreneurship Adjunct Faculty Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites Job Responsibilities: The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina is seeking applicants for adjunct faculty in Management and Entrepreneurship disciplines in the Baker School of Business. Our goal is to build long-term relationships with high-quality adjunct part-time faculty members who share in The Citadel’s commitment to develop principled leaders in business. There are main programs where adjunct faculty may be employed to teach classes: Our traditional undergraduate program, which features face-to-face classes to the South Carolina Corps of Cadets Our part time undergraduate degree completion program, which are primarily working adults earning Bachelor’s degrees, mostly through online classes. Minimum Qualifications: To teach at the undergraduate level, applicants must have a minimum of a Master's degree from an AACSB-Accredited Institution in the appropriate business discipline or in a closely related field. Be able to teach in-person classes, on campus in Charleston, SC. Evidence of previous effective teaching experience is required. Complete Citadel instructor training and follow rules and regulations set by The Citadel Center for Excellence and Innovation in Teaching, Learning and Distance Education (CEITL&DE). Preference is given to applicants who meet AACSB Qualifications as a Scholarly Academic, Practice Academic, Scholarly Practitioner, or Instructional Practitioner. Official transcripts indicating education level and background check are required prior to employment. If you have questions, please contact Dr. James Bezjian at jbezjian@citadel.edu . This is a pooled position and roles are dependent on department need. The review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until filled. Start Your Application First Name (required) 40db5a25 Last Name (required) 4afc0cfe Email (required) 1655cc67 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
