    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-modern-languages-french-pooled-position-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Modern Languages - French (pooled position)",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Modern Languages - French (pooled position) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Adjunct Faculty - Modern Languages - French (pooled position) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty - Modern Languages - French (pooled position) Modern Language Adjunct Faculty Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites The Citadel's French Program welcomes applications for adjunct faculty instructors in French. Course availability varies. Subject to experience, teaching assignments may include beginner through intermediate language instruction. Scheduling is typically flexible within the weekday hours of 8 a.m. and 3 p.m. The Citadel’s goal is to build long-term relationships with high-quality part-time faculty members who are committed to developing principled, well-rounded leaders who appreciate the value of being culturally and linguistically proficient in world languages other than their own. This job posting is not for a specific assignment or for a full-time faculty position, but rather for a pool of candidates who may be considered. Minimum Qualifications: Native or near-native fluency in French Master's degree in French or a Master's degree in another subject with 18 hours of graduate-level study in French or an equivalent Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching at the undergraduate level Interested applicants should start by sending a brief letter of application and a CV to: Dr. Caroline Strobbe ( cstrobbe@citadel.edu ), Department of Modern Languages, Literatures, and Cultures, The Citadel. About The Citadel College The Citadel, also known as the Military College of South Carolina, is a public senior military college located in Charleston, South Carolina. Founded in 1842, The Citadel has a rich history and educational reputation. With our current location on the banks of the Ashley River in downtown Charleston, you are close to great restaurants, shopping and much more. Ranked #1 Public College in the South (U.S. News & World Report, 2022) for schools with up to a master’s degree, the opportunities are endless. There are about 2,300 undergraduate students who make up the South Carolina Corps of Cadets. Out of the Corps of Cadets, 1 out of 3 graduates earn a military commission. Students can choose from 31 Majors, 57 Minors, pre-health professions, and pre-law (a concentration in political science). The 11:1 student-to-faculty ratio guarantees students a quality education. Another 1,000 students attend the Graduate College, evening and online programs. Start Your Application First Name (required) 5dde2667 Last Name (required) ac886074 Email (required) 6bb25fd0 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't 