    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-department-of-intelligence-and-security-studies-pooled-positions-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Department of Intelligence and Security Studies (pooled positions)",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Department of Intelligence and Security Studies (pooled positions) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Adjunct Faculty - Department of Intelligence and Security Studies (pooled positions) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty - Department of Intelligence and Security Studies (pooled positions) Intel & Security Studies Adjunct Faculty Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites Job Responsibilities: The Citadel's Department of Intelligence and Security Studies is establishing a pool of applicants to fill potential part-time teaching positions for undergraduate and/or graduate positions. Courses are offered during the day and online throughout the academic year (fall, spring, and summer). All adjunct positions are per session appointments. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: - Abiding by and upholding the Citadel's mission, policies, and core values. - Utilizing effective teaching and learning practices such as presentations, demonstrations, class discussion, and other appropriate modes of instructional delivery. - Preparing course outlines and syllabi in accordance with program standards and in collaboration with the program coordinator. - Completing student assessments required for program completion. - Meeting all scheduled class periods, being available to students for individual consultations, submitting grades by the specified due date. - The Citadel requires faculty to submit midterm grades for undergraduate students as well as utilize the Attendance and Class Absence System for undergraduate students. Minimum Qualifications: - Doctoral degree is required to teach graduate courses and a Master's degree is required to teach undergraduate courses. - Three years teaching experience at the elementary, middle grades, secondary, and/or college level. - Excellent written and oral communication skills. - Exceptional interpersonal and collaboration skills. - Experience in designing courses and materials. In addition to the online application, please provide a cover letter and CV. Start Your Application First Name (required) 9363bde3 Last Name (required) 6c887749 Email (required) 0210fc8a Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-in-the-department-of-cyber-and-computer-sciences-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty in the Department of Cyber and Computer Sciences",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty in the Department of Cyber and Computer Sciences - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Adjunct Faculty in the Department of Cyber and Computer Sciences - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty in the Department of Cyber and Computer Sciences Cyber and Computer Sciences Adjunct Faculty Add to favorites View favorites The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina is seeking applicants for adjunct faculty in the Department of Cyber and Computer Sciences. Our goal is to build long-term relationships with high-quality adjunct part-time faculty members from Industry who share in the Citadel commitment to develop principled leaders in Cyber and Computer Sciences. Job Responsibilities: There are three main programs that adjunct faculty may be employed to teach classes: Traditional undergraduate program, which features face-to-face classes to the South Carolina Corps of Cadets Undergraduate evening 2+2 programs, which are primarily working adults earning Bachelor’s degrees Our joint graduate evening programs in Computer and Information Sciences with College of Charleston. We have ongoing needs to fill vacancies in one or more of the following areas: Cybersecurity Cyber Operations Software Engineering Web Programming Minimum Qualifications: To teach at the undergraduate level, applicants must have a minimum of a Master's degree from an Accredited Institution in the Computer Science/Information Systems/Cybersecurity discipline or in a closely related field To teach at the graduate level, applicants must hold a terminal degree in the field from an Accredited Institution in the Computer Science/Information Systems/Cybersecurity discipline or in a closely related field Preference will be given to applicants who have previous effective teaching experience. Official transcripts indicating education level are required prior to employment. If you have questions, please contact Dr. Shankar Banik by phone at: 843-953-5039, or by email at: shankar.banik@citadel.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until all positions are filled. Start Your Application First Name (required) 9afc8a14 Last Name (required) e9ccf7b4 Email (required) c5ecdb76 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
