    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-in-fine-arts-citadel-s-department-of-english-fine-arts-and-communications-pooled-position-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty in Fine Arts - Citadel's Department of English, Fine Arts, and Communications (pooled position)",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty in Fine Arts - Citadel's Department of English, Fine Arts, and Communications (pooled position) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Adjunct Faculty in Fine Arts - Citadel's Department of English, Fine Arts, and Communications (pooled position) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty in Fine Arts - Citadel's Department of English, Fine Arts, and Communications (pooled position) English Fine Arts and Comm Adjunct Faculty Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites Job Responsibilities: The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolina is currently accepting applications to establish a pool for adjunct faculty assignments. Adjunct assignments may be temporary, part-time and/or on-call and may be immediate or as needed. This job posting is not for a specific assignment or for a full-time faculty position, but rather for a pool of candidates who may be considered for part-time teaching or allied faculty assignments. The Citadel’s Department of English, Fine Arts, and Communications is establishing a pool of applicants in the Fine Arts. Duties include teaching undergraduate course(s) in one or more of the following areas: Theatre, Cultural Preservation, 3-D Technologies, Photography, Photoshop, Forensic Photography, or other Fine Arts disciplines, based on departmental needs. Undergraduate courses are offered during the day in face-to-face or hyflex formats throughout the academic year (fall, spring, and summer). All adjunct positions are part-time, temporary, and per session appointments. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Abiding by and upholding the Citadel’s mission, policies, and core values. Utilizing effective teaching and learning practices such as presentations, demonstrations, class discussion, and other appropriate modes of instructional delivery; preparing course outlines and syllabi in accordance with program standards and in collaboration with the program coordinator. Completing student assessments required for program completion; hosting weekly office hours; meeting all scheduled class periods. Being available to students for individual consultation; submitting midterm grades; recording class absences and submitting final grades by the specified due date. The Citadel requires faculty to submit midterm grades for undergraduate students. The Citadel requires faculty to use the Attendance and Class Absence System to document class attendance for most undergraduate students. Minimum Qualifications: A Master’s Degree in a related Fine Arts field (such as Theatre, Photography, Graphic Design, Studio Art, or Art History) is required to teach undergraduate courses. Previous effective teaching at the high school or college level is required. Exceptional interpersonal and collaboration skills. Preferred Qualifications: Professional experience in the field is preferred. Experience in designing courses and materials for face-to-face and online formats is preferred. Start Your Application First Name (required) 573b6cf3 Last Name (required) 9f79940c Email (required) ef6d3b0d Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
