    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-chemistry-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Chemistry",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Chemistry - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Adjunct Faculty - Chemistry - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty - Chemistry Chemistry Adjunct Faculty Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites The Citadel, The Military College of South Carolinas is establishing a pool of applicants to teach in the Chemistry Department. Our goal is to build long-term relationships with high-quality part-time faculty members who share in The Citadel’s commitment to developing principled, well-rounded leaders. Duties may include teaching graduate and undergraduate courses. Minimum Qualifications Applicants must have a MS or PhD in chemistry or similar field; must have a minimum of 18 credit hours in graduate-level chemistry/biochemistry courses. College teaching experience is desirable. Necessary materials in addition to the online application (this can be attached to the online application) A curriculum vita Three letters of professional reference Start Your Application First Name (required) be8c86e0 Last Name (required) 7938373e Email (required) a5a637a1 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
