    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-supply-chain-management-baker-school-of-business-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty (Supply Chain Management) - Baker School of Business",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty (Supply Chain Management) - Baker School of Business - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Adjunct Faculty (Supply Chain Management) - Baker School of Business - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty (Supply Chain Management) - Baker School of Business Mktg Supl Chain and Econ Adjunct Faculty 2950 Add to favorites View favorites Adjunct Instructor Position in Supply Chain Management The Citadel’s Tommy and Victoria Baker School of Business continues to grow! The Citadel is ranked the #1 Public College in the South offering up to a master’s degree twelve consecutive years and one of the Ten Best Undergraduate Teaching Schools in the South by U.S. News and World Report . We have innovative new academic programs, and a new business building, Bastin Hall, that opened Spring 2021. The ideal candidate will contribute to in-person, face-to-face course offerings and asynchronous online course offerings in Supply Chain Management at the undergraduate level. The Baker School of Business is AACSB-accredited and offers a traditional residential undergraduate program to members of the South Carolina Corps of Cadets (SCCC) in a military-college setting an undergraduate degree completion program. Job Responsibilities: The Baker School of Business invites applications for an adjunct position in Supply Chain Management. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses using both traditional and online delivery methods. The teaching load for this position is one to two courses per semester. Opportunities for summer teaching and additional compensation may also arise. Minimum Requirements: Applicants must have an earned Master’s Degree in a business discipline from an AACSB-accredited university , have relevant industry experience in the discipline, and be qualified to teach courses in Supply Chain Management at the undergraduate level. Preferred Qualifications: Candidates holding a PhD or DBA from an AACSB-accredited university are highly encouraged to apply. Online teaching experience in Canvas LMS is preferred but not required. Preference will be given to candidates with the ability to teach one or more of the following courses: Principles of Operations Management, Quality Management, Supply Chain Management, Logistics Management, Purchasing and Materials Management, or SAP-related Special Topics Courses . Relevant experience in industry, the military, or other organizational contexts is preferred but not required. Next Steps Interested applicants should utilize the official online application website and please upload supporting documents to include: Letter of interest addressing the qualifications listed above A curriculum vita Evidence of teaching effectiveness Contact information for at least three professional references. Additional Comments: Initial screening of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. This is a civilian, non-uniform, position. About the Institution The Citadel , also known as the Military College of South Carolina, is a public senior military college located in Charleston, South Carolina . Founded in 1842, The Citadel has a rich history and a heritage of excellence in education, emphasizing leadership development. The Citadel provides a unique, residential undergraduate experience in a military-college setting. There are approximately 2,300 undergraduate students who make up the South Carolina Corps of Cadets. Nearly one-third of our SCCC graduates earn a military commission in one of the five US Military Branches. Students can choose from 31 Majors and 57 Minors. The 11:1 student-to-faculty ratio guarantees students a quality education. Another 1,000 students, including MBA students, attend programs in the nonresidential Citadel Graduate College. The Citadel is located on the banks of the Ashley River near downtown Charleston, and is close to great restaurants and shopping , and much more. Life on The Citadel’s campus is the best way to work in Charleston. Stop into the full-service Starbucks on campus before the day begins. Between the parade deck (Summerall Field) and Hampton Park, right next to campus, one has access to the largest amount of green space on the peninsula. Start Your Application First Name (required) e181dbf3 Last Name (required) 4186f6ec Email (required) 83ba9c74 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-teacher-education-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Teacher Education",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Teacher Education - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Adjunct Faculty - Teacher Education - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty - Teacher Education Zucker Family School of Ed Adjunct Faculty Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites Job Responsibilities: The Citadel’s Zucker Family School of Education invites applicants for an adjunct faculty position in the Division of Teacher Education to be filled for the fall and spring semesters this year and in the future. The selected applicant will teach day classes in our undergraduate programs that lead to initial teacher certification in the areas of social studies, biology, chemistry, and physical education. Based on need and qualifications, there might be opportunity to teach in our MAT program in the evenings which leads to initial teacher certification in the areas of social studies, biology, mathematics, English, and physical education. These courses include topics on child development, adolescent development, peer counseling, methods, educational pyschology, etc. Minimum Qualifications: An earned doctorate from an accredited university in teacher education, curriculum and instruction, educational psychology, child development or related field; demonstrated success as a P-12 teacher and/or P-12 certified professional; ability to use and model technology as an instructional tool; ability to collaborate with local P-12 school districts; and preparing professional educators to work in school environments. Preferred Qualifications: Teaching skills that employ a variety of instructional strategies in both face-to-face and online environments as well as previous experience teaching at the collegiate level. Please contact Dr. Christopher T. Dague by phone at 843-953-2064 or by email at cdague@citadel.edu for any questions or further information. Start Your Application First Name (required) 2beb6c17 Last Name (required) ec5c7c84 Email (required) 297e5388 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
