    "https://jobs.citadel.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-m-ed-in-higher-education-leadership-program-pooled-position-charleston-south-carolina-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - M.Ed. in Higher Education Leadership Program (pooled position)",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - M.Ed. in Higher Education Leadership Program (pooled position) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Adjunct Faculty - M.Ed. in Higher Education Leadership Program (pooled position) - Charleston, South Carolina, United States Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty - M.Ed. in Higher Education Leadership Program (pooled position) Zucker Family School of Ed Adjunct Faculty Unclassified Add to favorites View favorites M.Ed. in Higher Education Leadership The Citadel’s Zucker Family School of Education (ZFSOE) is establishing a pool of applicants to fill potential part-time temporary online teaching positions within the M.Ed. in Higher Education Leadership Program. All adjunct positions are per session appointments. The program is seeking adjuncts with expertise to facilitate the following courses: EDUC 622 Critical Multicultural Issues in Higher Education EDUC 562 Legal & Ethical Leadership Issues in Education EDUC 634 Practicum in Higher Education Administration EDUC 655 Internship in Higher Education Administration Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Abiding by and upholding the Citadel’s mission, policies, and core values. Utilizing effective online teaching and learning practices. Preparing course materials and syllabi in accordance with program standards and in collaboration with the program coordinator. Being available to students for individual consultation, providing constructive feedback, and submitting final grades by the specified due date. Minimum Qualifications: A doctoral degree in Higher Education Administration, Student Affairs, or a closely related field is required. Previous online teaching experience is required. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Exceptional interpersonal and collaboration skills. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in designing online courses and materials is preferred. In addition to the online application, please provide a cover letter and CV. Start Your Application First Name (required) 3ae10825 Last Name (required) b951eb3e Email (required) 596495b2 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you. You'll be redirected to login and continue your application! Recommended Jobs HVAC Technician Charleston Facilities & Engineering The Citadel is currently looking for a skilled HVAC person. If you are interested, please apply now! Assistant Professor of Intelligence and Security Studies Charleston Intel & Security Studies The Department of Intelligence and Security Studies at The Citadel invites applications for a full-time, [nine-month, tenure-track] Assistant Professor with expertise in irregular warfare, beginning August 2027. We seek a colleague who will bring original scholarship and imaginative teaching to a department helping students understand the exercise of power and prepare for the responsibilities of national security work. Please Note: Due to recent federal changes with H1B visa fees, The Citadel is currently not sponsoring new H1B applications. Legal & Compliance Accessibility Privacy Copyright © 2026 The Citadel Cookie Preferences Candidate Details We use cookies. Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site . Accept essential only Accept all"
